mulation -- 94-- `--engine`: `gromacs` (default) / `mace`. `mace` = ASE + MACE-MP Langevin NVT (fixed-seed box, 298.15 K, 1 fs step), requires only mace-torch, no GROMACS/.itp templates; for Top-1 cross-validation run both engines and compare D_Li_m2_s. 95-- Output: `{"D_Li_m2_s": f, "trajectory_ok": bool, "drift_check": "ok"|"drift"|"skipped", "achieved_density_g_cm3": f}` — on `trajectory_ok: false` (drift) record and report honestly (mace drift criterion = last-20% mean MACE potential energy drifting > 5% from the middle segment) 96-- Errors: 97-  - `unknown engine 'x'; legal: gromacs, mace` → fix engine name 98-  - `GROMACS not found; install via winget install GROMACS.GROMACS or conda` → install GROMACS (gromacs engine only) 99-  - `mace engine requires mace-torch; install via \`pip install mace-torch\`` → install mace-torch (mace engine only) 100-  - `box must contain at least 1 Li` → box needs ≥ 1 Li 101-  - `missing OPLS-AA .itp template(s): ...` → generate the corresponding .itp templates per the skill's `scripts/bda/simulators/data/opls/README.md` (gromacs engine only) 102-  - `gmx mdrun failed: ...` / `gmx trjconv failed: ...` → troubleshoot per trailing stderr content 103- 104:## render — HTML report 105- 106-``` 107:bda render --case-dir CASE_DIR [--out OUT] 108-``` 109- 110-- Reads `<case_dir>/log.jsonl` (entry 0 criteria + all action entries), produces a self-contained HTML (task overview / iteration trajectory / funnel statistics / stage results / true DFT-MD endorsement / final recommendation / design notes — seven sections), written to `<case_dir>/<out>` (default `report.html`) 111:- No log.jsonl → renders an empty report; no corresponding entry → section shows "no data yet" 112-- Errors: no custom validation; log-line JSON parse failure → traceback pointing at the line number 113-- Where used: last closing step; report content deterministically generated from log.jsonl, no extra LLM calls 114- 115-## run-comp — electrode composition screening (CHG